	(text "GAIN register (4h) reset = 0x0001 = 0–5 V range.\nWrite 0x0101 (REF-DIV=1, BUFF-GAIN=1) → 0–2.5 V DAC, 0–3.300 V at AOUT.\nDo this before any DAC data write.\nREF-DIV=0 puts VREFIO at exactly 0.5 × VDD and trips the reference alarm if the 5 V rail sags\n— the alarm shuts the reference buffer down and forces the output to 0 V,\nwhich reads as a valid end-of-travel angle."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 162.052 87.63 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "60530ca5-c32c-4ae6-8559-0511f4d8a58a")
	)
	(text "2-POLE SALLEN-KEY RECONSTRUCTION / ANTI-ALIAS FILTER\n  f0 = 1/(2*pi*C*sqrt(R35006*R35007))     C35008 = C35009 = C\n  1/Q = 1/sqrt(a) + sqrt(a)*(2-K),  a = R35006/R35007,  K = 1.32\n  AS BUILT: 20.0k / 13.0k / 10nF x2  ->  f0 = 987 Hz, Q = 0.606, -3dB 827 Hz\n\nWHY IT EXISTS: acquisition (OneBox, AD7616) samples at a FIXED 30.3 kHz behind\nonly a 1st-order 39 kHz filter, so it does not antialias. The TMC5130A chopper\nruns 16-30 kHz (datasheet-recommended range) and EVERY value in that range\nfolds into 0-15 kHz, where it is indistinguishable from joystick motion. This\nfilter is the only band limit in the chain. It also cuts the DAC code-change\nglitch from 9.9 mV to 14 uV. OneBox LSB = 152.6 uV on the +/-5 V range.\n\nTO RETUNE: scale R35006 AND R35007 by the SAME factor. Q depends only on their\nratio (1.538), so shape is preserved and only f0 moves. Do not change C.\n  64.9k/42.2k   304 Hz  -72.7dB@20k  864us delay\n  39.2k/25.5k   503 Hz  -64.0dB@20k  522us\n  20.0k/13.0k   987 Hz  -52.3dB@20k  266us   <-- DEFAULT\n  9.76k/6.34k  2.02 kHz -39.8dB@20k  130us\n  6.49k/4.22k  3.04 kHz -32.7dB@20k   86us\n  3.92k/2.55k  5.03 kHz -24.0dB@20k   52us\n  2.00k/1.30k  9.87 kHz -13.2dB@20k   27us   (chopper barely attenuated)\n\nSINGLE-POLE FALLBACK (same pads): R35006 = 0R jumper, C35008 = DNP,\n  R35007 = 15.0k, C35009 = 10nF  ->  1.061 kHz, 1 pole, -25.5dB@20k, 150us.\n  C35008 MUST be DNP in this configuration - with R35006 shorted it would hang\n  10nF from the DAC output to the op-amp output.\n\nCONSTRAINTS\n - C0G ONLY. Class-2 dielectric is piezoelectric and this board sits next to a\n   stepper; the series R can only bleed self-generated charge with time constant\n   R*C, which is fixed by f0, so it cannot be filtered away.\n   (TI DACx0501 datasheet 9.2.2.6.)\n - C35008 and C35009 must be the SAME value and ideally the same reel. Q depends\n   on C35008/C35009 = 1; matched caps make Q immune to cap tolerance.\n - R35006/R35007 carry no DC current (op-amp Ib = 10 pA), so DC gain is set\n   ENTIRELY by R35001/R35002. +/-1% here is plenty; do not \"upgrade\" to 0.1%.\n - Keep C35004 = 10pF. Its pole is at 4.97 MHz and it rolls K toward 1.0 at HF,\n   which lowers Q up there - stabilizing, not destabilizing.\n - Do not put the shunt cap on the BNC side of R35004. A cap large enough to\n   matter there (640nF for 1 kHz) drives U35001 into its +/-65 mA limit on every\n   step, and its corner would track the researcher's cable capacitance.\n - Group delay is a latency you must MEASURE and report, not assume.\n - Sallen-Key stopband floors out above ~1 MHz as the op-amp output impedance\n   rises and C35008 stops bootstrapping. Irrelevant at 16-30 kHz.\n\nLAYOUT: keep FLT_MID and FLT_IN short and surrounded by analog GND."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
